{"id":"mahabharata-12-075","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":75,"title":"पञ्चसप्ततितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 75 · Mucukunda and Kubera","summary":{"en":"Bhishma says the realm's welfare rests on the king's care for the poor, and tells how King Mucukunda defeated Kubera's rakshasas by his own righteousness. He says that brahmins and Kshatriyas must always work together for the good of the people.","kn":"ರಾಜ್ಯದ ಕ್ಷೇಮ ರಾಜನ ಬಡವರ ಆರೈಕೆಯ ಮೇಲೆ ನಿಂತಿದೆ; ರಾಜ ಮುಚುಕುಂದ ತನ್ನ ಧರ್ಮದಿಂದ ಕುಬೇರನ ರಾಕ್ಷಸರನ್ನು ಗೆದ್ದ ಕಥೆ ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣರು, ಕ್ಷತ್ರಿಯರು ಜನರ ಹಿತಕ್ಕಾಗಿ ಯಾವಾಗಲೂ ಒಟ್ಟಾಗಿ ಕೆಲಸ ಮಾಡಬೇಕು.","hi":"भीष्म कहते हैं कि राज्य का कल्याण राजा द्वारा निर्धनों की देखभाल पर निर्भर है, और बताते हैं कि राजा मुचुकुन्द ने अपने धर्म से कुबेर के राक्षसों को जीता। वे कहते हैं कि ब्राह्मण और क्षत्रिय प्रजा के हित के लिए सदा साथ काम करें।","te":"రాజ్య క్షేమం రాజు పేదల సంరక్షణపై ఆధారపడిందని, రాజు ముచుకుందుడు తన ధర్మంతో కుబేరుని రాక్షసులను గెలిచిన కథను భీష్ముడు చెబుతాడు. బ్రాహ్మణులు, క్షత్రియులు ప్రజల హితం కోసం ఎల్లప్పుడూ కలిసి పని చేయాలంటాడు.","ta":"நாட்டின் நலம் மன்னன் ஏழைகளைப் பேணுவதில் உள்ளது, மன்னன் முசுகுந்தன் தன் தர்மத்தால் குபேரனின் அரக்கரை வென்ற கதையைப் பீஷ்மர் கூறுகிறார். அந்தணரும் க்ஷத்திரியரும் மக்கள் நலனுக்காக எப்போதும் இணைந்து செயல்பட வேண்டும் என்கிறார்.","ml":"രാജ്യത്തിന്റെ ക്ഷേമം ദരിദ്രരെക്കുറിച്ചുള്ള രാജാവിന്റെ കരുതലിലാണെന്ന് ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു; മുചുകുന്ദൻ രാജാവ് സ്വന്തം ധർമ്മബോധത്താൽ കുബേരന്റെ രാക്ഷസന്മാരെ തോൽപ്പിച്ചതെങ്ങനെയെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം വിവരിക്കുന്നു. ജനങ്ങളുടെ നന്മയ്ക്കായി ബ്രാഹ്മണരും ക്ഷത്രിയരും എപ്പോഴും ഒത്തുചേർന്ന് പ്രവർത്തിക്കണമെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.75; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"राजधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Rajadharma Parva (Duties of kings)","verses":[{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"योगक्षेमो हि राष्ट्रस्य राजन्यायत्त उच्यते ।\nयोगक्षेमश्च राज्ञोऽपि समायत्तः पुरोहिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, the gaining and keeping of goods in the kingdom is said to depend on the king, and the king's own depends on his household priest."}},{"n":2,"text":"यतादृष्टं भयं ब्रह्म प्रजानां शमयत्युत ।\nदृष्टं च राजा बाहुभ्यां तद्राष्ट्रं सुखमेधते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmana power calms the fears that are unseen to the people, and the king calms those that are seen with his arms; so that kingdom prospers happily."}},{"n":3,"text":"अत्राप्युदाहरन्तीममितिहासं पुरातनम् ।\nमुचुकुन्दस्य संवादं राज्ञो वैश्रवणस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"On this they cite an ancient tale, the conversation between King Muchukunda and Vaishravana."}},{"n":4,"text":"मुचुकुन्दो विजित्येमां पृथिवीं पृथिवीपतिः ।\nजिज्ञासमानः स्वबलमभ्ययादलकाधिपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Muchukunda, lord of the earth, having conquered this earth, went to test his own strength against the lord of Alaka."}},{"n":5,"text":"ततो वैश्रवणो राजा रक्षांसि समवासृजत् ।\nते बलान्यवमृद्नन्तः प्राचरंस्तस्य नैरृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Vaishravana sent out rakshasas, and those night-wanderers moved about, crushing his armies."}},{"n":6,"text":"स हन्यमाने सैन्ये स्वे मुचुकुन्दो नराधिपः ।\nगर्हयामास विद्वांसं पुरोहितमरिंदमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As his army was being slain, King Muchukunda, tamer of foes, rebuked his learned household priest."}},{"n":7,"text":"तत उग्रं तपस्तप्त्वा वसिष्ठो ब्रह्मवित्तमः ।\nरक्षांस्यपावधीत्तत्र पन्थानं चाप्यविन्दत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Vasishtha, best among knowers of Brahman, performed fierce austerity, killed the rakshasas there and found a way out."}},{"n":8,"text":"ततो वैश्रवणो राजा मुचुकुन्दमदर्शयत् ।\nवध्यमानेषु सैन्येषु वचनं चेदमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Vaishravana showed himself to Muchukunda, while the armies were still being struck, and said these words."}},{"n":9,"text":"त्वत्तो हि बलिनः पूर्वे राजानः सपुरोहिताः ।\nन चैवं समवर्तंस्ते यथा त्वमिह वर्तसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Earlier kings with priests, mightier than you, did not behave as you do here."}},{"n":10,"text":"ते खल्वपि कृतास्त्राश्च बलवन्तश्च भूमिपाः ।\nआगम्य पर्युपासन्ते मामीशं सुखदुःखयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those armed and powerful rulers of the earth came to me and served me as lord in joy and sorrow."}},{"n":11,"text":"यद्यस्ति बाहुवीर्यं ते तद्दर्शयितुमर्हसि ।\nकिं ब्राह्मणबलेन त्वमतिमात्रं प्रवर्तसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you have strength of arm, you should show it; why do you act so excessively, relying on Brahmana power?"}},{"n":12,"text":"मुचुकुन्दस्ततः क्रुद्धः प्रत्युवाच धनेश्वरम् ।\nन्यायपूर्वमसंरब्धमसंभ्रान्तमिदं वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Muchukunda, angered, answered the lord of wealth with these words, proper, calm and unflustered."}},{"n":13,"text":"ब्रह्मक्षत्रमिदं सृष्टमेकयोनि स्वयंभुवा ।\nपृथग्बलविधानं च तल्लोकं परिरक्षति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The priestly and warrior powers were made by the Self-born from one womb, and their separate arrangement of strength protects the world."}},{"n":14,"text":"तपोमन्त्रबलं नित्यं ब्राह्मणेषु प्रतिष्ठितम् ।\nअस्त्रबाहुबलं नित्यं क्षत्रियेषु प्रतिष्ठितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The strength of austerity and mantras is ever established in Brahmanas; the strength of weapons and arms is ever established in Kshatriyas."}},{"n":15,"text":"ताभ्यां संभूय कर्तव्यं प्रजानां परिपालनम् ।\nतथा च मां प्रवर्तन्तं गर्हयस्यलकाधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"The protection of the people must be done by the two together; and you blame me for acting thus, lord of Alaka."}},{"n":16,"text":"ततोऽब्रवीद्वैश्रवणो राजानं सपुरोहितम् ।\nनाहं राज्यमनिर्दिष्टं कस्मैचिद्विदधाम्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Vaishravana said to the king and his priest: I do not give a kingdom to anyone unassigned."}},{"n":17,"text":"नाच्छिन्दे चापि निर्दिष्टमिति जानीहि पार्थिव ।\nप्रशाधि पृथिवीं वीर मद्दत्तामखिलामिमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nor do I take away what has been assigned; know this, king. Hero, rule this whole earth, which is given by me."}},{"text":"मुचुकुन्द उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Muchukunda said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"नाहं राज्यं भवद्दत्तं भोक्तुमिच्छामि पार्थिव ।\nबाहुवीर्यार्जितं राज्यमश्नीयामिति कामये ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, I do not wish to enjoy a kingdom given by you; I wish to enjoy a kingdom won by the strength of my own arms."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":19,"text":"ततो वैश्रवणो राजा विस्मयं परमं ययौ ।\nक्षत्रधर्मे स्थितं दृष्ट्वा मुचुकुन्दमसंभ्रमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Vaishravana was greatly astonished to see Muchukunda standing firm in the Kshatriya duty and unshaken."}},{"n":20,"text":"ततो राजा मुचुकुन्दः सोऽन्वशासद्वसुंधराम् ।\nबाहुवीर्यार्जितां सम्यक्क्षत्रधर्ममनुव्रतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Muchukunda ruled the earth, won by the strength of his own arms, faithful to the Kshatriya duty."}},{"n":21,"text":"एवं यो ब्रह्मविद्राजा ब्रह्मपूर्वं प्रवर्तते ।\nजयत्यविजितामुर्वीं यशश्च महदश्नुते ॥","meaning":{"en":"So the king who knows Brahman and acts with the priestly power first, wins the unconquered earth and attains great fame."}},{"n":22,"text":"नित्योदको ब्राह्मणः स्यान्नित्यशस्त्रश्च क्षत्रियः ।\nतयोर्हि सर्वमायत्तं यत्किंचिज्जगतीगतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Brahmana should always keep water at hand and the Kshatriya always keep his weapon; on these two all that exists on earth depends."}}]}]}